<ac:structured-macro ac:name="details"><ac:parameter ac:name="id">dbsec-platform</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><table><tbody><tr><th><p>Platform</p></th><td><p>Microsoft SQL Server</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Product</p></th><td><p>Microsoft SQL Server (Database Engine, on Windows or Linux; Always On availability groups)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Versions in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[e.g., 2019, 2022]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Policy</p></th><td><p><code>SEC-POL-DB-001</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Technical basis</p></th><td><p>CIS Microsoft SQL Server 2019 / 2022 Benchmark</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable audit file(s)</p></th><td><p>CIS_Microsoft_SQL_Server_2022_*.audit (database checks) + Windows audit for registry / service checks</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Tenable credential</p></th><td><p>Database credential, type SQL Server (Windows or SQL authentication; one entry per instance / port)</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Control prefix</p></th><td><p><code>MSSQL</code></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Instances in scope</p></th><td><p><em>[count or link to CMDB]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Controls</p></th><td><p>15</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Automated (Tenable)</p></th><td><p>10 of 15</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Compliance % (last scan)</p></th><td><p>0%</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Open CRITICAL / HIGH</p></th><td><p>0</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Last Tenable scan</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Owner team</p></th><td><p><em>[Team]</em></p></td></tr><tr><th><p>Next review due</p></th><td><p>YYYY-MM-DD</p></td></tr></tbody></table></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="warning"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">Company policy – SEC-POL-DB-001</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><p>This page is part of the company Database Security Configuration Policy (SEC-POL-DB-001). Its requirements are mandatory for every database in scope. Deviations need an approved entry in the DB Security – Exceptions Register. CIS Benchmarks and Tenable audit files are the technical basis and assessment method; where this policy differs from CIS, this policy applies.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="toc"><ac:parameter ac:name="maxLevel">2</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>
<h2>Scope &amp; applicability</h2>
<ul><li>Instance-level controls apply to every instance, including named instances and SSRS / SSAS hosts where a Database Engine is installed.</li><li>Database-level controls (guest, TRUSTWORTHY, TDE) apply to every user database; system databases are noted in Comments.</li><li>Azure SQL Database / Managed Instance: controls the platform enforces are N/A.</li></ul>
<h2>Tenable assessment setup</h2>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Item</p></th><th><p>Value</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan template</strong></p></td><td><p>Policy Compliance Auditing (credentialed)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Audit file(s)</strong></p></td><td><p>CIS_Microsoft_SQL_Server_2022_*.audit (database checks) + Windows audit for registry / service checks</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Credential</strong></p></td><td><p>Database credential, type SQL Server (Windows or SQL authentication; one entry per instance / port)</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Scan account privileges</strong></p></td><td><p><code>VIEW SERVER STATE</code>, <code>VIEW ANY DEFINITION</code>, <code>CONNECT ANY DATABASE</code> (2014+), membership of the user role in <code>msdb</code>; no sysadmin</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Tailoring</strong></p></td><td><p>Company values from the register below override CIS defaults in the tailored audit file. Store it in <em>[repository / Tenable policy name]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Control register</h2>
<ac:structured-macro ac:name="info"><ac:parameter ac:name="title">How to maintain this register</ac:parameter><ac:rich-text-body><ul><li>One row per control. Control IDs are never renumbered or reused.</li><li><strong>Tenable Check</strong> describes what the audit item reads and its pass condition. Copy the CIS section from the audit item's <code>reference</code> field into <strong>CIS Reference</strong>.</li><li>Changing a Compliant Value is a policy change: record it in the change log and get approval.</li><li>After every scan, update Compliance % and Open CRITICAL / HIGH in the table at the top of the page.</li></ul></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>
<table><tbody><tr><th><p>Control ID</p></th><th><p>Control Name</p></th><th><p>Domain</p></th><th><p>Requirement</p></th><th><p>Severity</p></th><th><p>Compliant Value</p></th><th><p>Tenable Check (Audit / Query)</p></th><th><p>CIS Reference</p></th><th><p>Assessment</p></th><th><p>Last Review (Date / By)</p></th><th><p>Comments</p></th></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-VER-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Supported version with latest CU / GDR</p></td><td><p><code>VER</code></p></td><td><p>The instance runs a supported version with the latest security update (CU or GDR) within the patch SLA.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>SERVERPROPERTY('ProductUpdateLevel')</code> matches the approved build list</p></td><td><p><code>SELECT @@VERSION</code>; compared with the approved build list</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Tenable vulnerability plugins also flag missing updates.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-AAA-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Windows authentication mode</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Instances use Windows Authentication only. Mixed mode needs an approved exception.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>SERVERPROPERTY('IsIntegratedSecurityOnly')</code> = 1</p></td><td><p>Query <code>SERVERPROPERTY</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-AAA-002</strong></p></td><td><p>sa disabled and renamed</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>The built-in sa login (principal_id 1) is disabled and renamed.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>sys.server_principals</code> where <code>principal_id = 1</code>: <code>is_disabled = 1</code>, name ≠ 'sa'</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.server_principals</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-AAA-003</strong></p></td><td><p>SQL logins follow password policy</p></td><td><p><code>AAA</code></p></td><td><p>Every SQL-authenticated login enforces the Windows password policy; expiration is enforced for logins in sysadmin.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>is_policy_checked = 1</code> for all SQL logins; <code>is_expiration_checked = 1</code> for sysadmin members</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.sql_logins</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-SVC-001</strong></p></td><td><p>xp_cmdshell disabled</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>xp_cmdshell must be disabled.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Red</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">CRITICAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>xp_cmdshell</code> value_in_use = 0</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.configurations</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-SVC-002</strong></p></td><td><p>Surface-area options disabled</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>Server options that extend the attack surface are disabled unless approved.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>value_in_use = 0 for <code>Ad Hoc Distributed Queries</code>, <code>clr enabled</code>, <code>cross db ownership chaining</code>, <code>Database Mail XPs</code>, <code>Ole Automation Procedures</code>, <code>remote access</code>, <code>scan for startup procs</code>; <code>clr strict security</code> = 1</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.configurations</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Database Mail is often required; record approved instances as exceptions.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-SVC-003</strong></p></td><td><p>Remote DAC restricted</p></td><td><p><code>SVC</code></p></td><td><p>The remote dedicated admin connection is off, except on clustered instances where it is needed.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>remote admin connections</code> = 0 (1 allowed on failover cluster instances)</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.configurations</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-PRIV-001</strong></p></td><td><p>guest has no CONNECT in user databases</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>The guest user cannot connect to any database other than master, tempdb and msdb.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>No <code>CONNECT</code> granted to guest in user databases</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.database_permissions</code> in each database</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-PRIV-002</strong></p></td><td><p>PUBLIC role has only default permissions</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>No permissions are granted to the public server role beyond the defaults; sysadmin members match the approved list.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Only default public grants (VIEW ANY DATABASE, CONNECT on default endpoints)</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.server_permissions</code> for grantee_principal_id = 2; list sysadmin members</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>sysadmin membership is compared with the approved list by the reviewer.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-PRIV-003</strong></p></td><td><p>TRUSTWORTHY off</p></td><td><p><code>PRIV</code></p></td><td><p>TRUSTWORTHY is OFF for every user database.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>is_trustworthy_on = 0</code> (msdb excepted)</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.databases</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-NET-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Instance not advertised</p></td><td><p><code>NET</code></p></td><td><p>The instance is hidden from SQL Browser enumeration and does not listen on the default port where feasible.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Grey</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">LOW</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>HideInstance = 1; static port other than 1433</p></td><td><p>Windows audit: registry check under <code>MSSQLServer\SuperSocketNetLib</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-CRYPTO-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Forced TLS encryption</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>Client connections are encrypted with TLS 1.2 or higher using a trusted certificate.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>ForceEncryption = 1; TLS 1.0 / 1.1 disabled in SCHANNEL</p></td><td><p>Windows audit: registry check on <code>SuperSocketNetLib\ForceEncryption</code> and SCHANNEL protocols</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Green</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">AUTOMATED</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-CRYPTO-002</strong></p></td><td><p>TDE for confidential databases</p></td><td><p><code>CRYPTO</code></p></td><td><p>Databases classified Confidential or higher use Transparent Data Encryption; certificates are backed up off-host.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><code>sys.dm_database_encryption_keys</code> encryption_state = 3</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.dm_database_encryption_keys</code></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>Data classification comes from the CMDB.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-LOG-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Login and security auditing</p></td><td><p><code>LOG</code></p></td><td><p>Failed and successful logins and security changes are audited and forwarded to the SIEM.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">HIGH</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Server audit spec with <code>FAILED_LOGIN_GROUP</code>, <code>SUCCESSFUL_LOGIN_GROUP</code>, <code>AUDIT_CHANGE_GROUP</code>; login auditing = Both</p></td><td><p>Query <code>sys.server_audit_specification_details</code>; registry AuditLevel = 3</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p>SIEM forwarding is confirmed manually by the SOC.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>MSSQL-OS-001</strong></p></td><td><p>Dedicated low-privilege service accounts</p></td><td><p><code>OS</code></p></td><td><p>Each SQL Server service runs under its own virtual, managed or domain account that is not a local or domain administrator.</p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Blue</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">MEDIUM</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p>Service accounts not in local Administrators; one account per service</p></td><td><p><code>sys.dm_server_services</code> + Windows audit group membership check</p></td><td><p><em>[CIS § from .audit]</em></p></td><td><p><ac:structured-macro ac:name="status"><ac:parameter ac:name="colour">Yellow</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name="title">PARTIAL</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p> </p></td></tr><tr><td><p><em>[MSSQL-DOMAIN-NNN]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Short control name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Domain]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[What must be true]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CRITICAL / HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Value that passes]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Audit item / query + pass condition]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[CIS §]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[AUTOMATED / PARTIAL / MANUAL / PLANNED / NOT FEASIBLE]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[YYYY-MM-DD / Name]</em></p></td><td><p><em>[Caveats, exception IDs]</em></p></td></tr></tbody></table>
